  "report_discrepancies": [{"check": "totals", "difference": 1, "source_page": 4, "note": "Governmental funds total revenues printed 1,087,136; total column lines add to 1,087,135 (rounding in intergovernmental/interest)."}, {"check": "business", "difference": 1, "source_page": 6, "note": "Nonoperating total printed (8,735) vs lines summing to (8,736); income before transfers printed (341,320) vs (341,321)."}, {"check": "balance", "difference": 1, "source_page": 1, "note": "Statement of Net Position: business-type asset lines add to 5,219,038 vs printed Business-type TOTAL ASSETS 5,219,039; certificates of deposit 162,205 + 2,304,897 = 2,467,102 vs printed Total 2,467,103 (page rounding). Split lines as printed sum to 6,511,755 vs printed total assets 6,511,756."}],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental totals from Total column p4; beginning balance is 'restated' 1,108,001. Beginning/ending cash = total fund balances. Business-type from proprietary statement p6 total column; no single total printed, so receipts/disbursements totals computed; misc revenues (expenses) shown net (2,734) in total column, recorded as a disbursement of 2,734. business_type measure net position (statement rolls net position). Balance sheet is government-wide total column p1. Detail: budget schedule for all funds (p7) mixes governmental and business-type, so fund_type assigned by line; charges for services and interest lines are mixed (review). Transfers out 371,224 inside printed total expenditures (includes other financing). Transfers in budget 140,000 has no actual. General fund combining schedule p8 not recorded in detail (duplicates the General Fund column of p4 split into sub-funds; total revenues 773,382 expenditures 651,910). Ending/beginning cash are the governmental total fund balances the statement rolls forward (p3-p4); the 1,135,138 includes Notes receivable 80,300 (Sales Tax Fund, p3), so governmental cash itself is 1,054,838 (881,870 + 162,205 + 10,763). Read pages 1-8 of 8."
}
